{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-10-15T01:22:26.839638Z", "id": "github:release:567038244:release:413002890", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 3952, "prerelease": true, "stars": 8347, "stars_delta": 9, "tag_name": "browser-demos-v6"}, "organization": "isaac-sim", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-10-14T17:37:14Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "567038244:release:413002890", "summary": "Prebuilt browser simulations for Isaac Lab documentation. Adds a compact 24-slab domino cascade, VBD cable bending, and Ant walking with steering and direct perturbations. Includes all earlier version directories unchanged.\n\nPhysics uses captured Newton Warp kernels compiled to CPU WebAssembly; Three.js renders the state and the shared JavaScript actor evaluates policy weights. The archive is served as static files and needs no simulation server.\n\n[Preview gallery](https://maxkra15.github.io/isaaclab-browser-demos/v6/) \u00b7 [Exporter reference #7974](https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/pull/7974) \u00b7 [Docs integration #8559](https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/pull/8559)\n\nDocumentation deployment verifies the accompanying SHA-256 before staging the archive. Serve extracted files over HTTP for local previews.\n", "title": "isaac-sim/IsaacLab Interactive browser demos v6", "topics": ["robot_learning", "robotics_mapping", "robotics_perception"], "updated_at": "2026-10-14T17:37:14Z", "url": "https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/releases/tag/browser-demos-v6", "venue": null}
{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-10-15T01:22:26.839638Z", "id": "github:release:567038244:release:412700518", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 3952, "prerelease": true, "stars": 8347, "stars_delta": 9, "tag_name": "browser-demos-v5"}, "organization": "isaac-sim", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-10-14T12:38:15Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "567038244:release:412700518", "summary": "MicroDuck warehouse interactions: convex colliders derived from enabled scene geometry, compound rack/pallet components, and 12 movable floor props. Other props and fixtures remain fixed. Free props use nominal 250 kg/m\u00b3 density and calculated mass/inertia.\n\nPhysics retains native BAM drives, the Newton constraint solver, 50 Hz policy control, and four 5 ms physics steps. Reset restores the captured robot and prop state. Robot/policy assets from v2 and warehouse visuals/textures from v4 are reused; v1\u2013v4 remain unchanged in this archive.\n\n[Play the preview](https://maxkra15.github.io/isaaclab-browser-demos/v5/?demo=microduck) \u00b7 [Exporter source #7974](https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/pull/7974) \u00b7 [Docs integration #8559](https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/pull/8559)\n\nSource revision: `2c6eda6d0e8065b1b0af998c6774369453fcc7a7`.\nArchive SHA-256: `08de8419b05815c629bc92d25826eee472cb6ee36d977f61611962ac977c4964`.\n\nValidated native observations/graph replay, browser contact-driven prop motion, gravity, reset, room containment, mouse/touch controls, and public preview loading/stepping. The docs workflow stages this checksum-pinned archive; it does not compile WASM.\n", "title": "isaac-sim/IsaacLab Browser demos v5", "topics": ["robot_learning", "robotics_mapping", "robotics_perception"], "updated_at": "2026-10-14T12:38:15Z", "url": "https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/releases/tag/browser-demos-v5", "venue": null}
{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-10-15T01:22:26.839638Z", "id": "github:release:567038244:release:412641599", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 3952, "prerelease": true, "stars": 8347, "stars_delta": 9, "tag_name": "browser-demos-v4"}, "organization": "isaac-sim", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-10-14T11:30:20Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "567038244:release:412641599", "summary": "Add edge-latched viewport joysticks and the bounded MicroDuck warehouse scene. Pull a stick back or press Escape to stop; arrows remain momentary. Turning from rest uses a visible 0.25 m/s forward assist. Robot dragging still applies 2 N.\n\nThe authored Factory meshes and base-color textures use 94 shared prototypes and 797 instances. The Newton/BAM simulation includes 25 static boxes for perimeter, shelf-row and clutter collisions. This is a browser adaptation of the scene, not the native training environment or complete warehouse dynamics. Original robot CAD and policy files reuse v2 assets.\n\nDeploy the complete archive: v1, v2 and v3 are unchanged and v4 reuses their files. Attribution and warehouse asset license notices are included. Exporters: [#7974](https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/pull/7974), source revision [0c89d1c46](https://github.com/maxkra15/IsaacLab/commit/0c89d1c460dbdf0bc066bd8be6e1d327bb1d9c18). Docs: [#8559](https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab/pull/8559).\n\nValidation: native/captured walking and observation checks; all twelve demos; mouse/touch latching, cancellation, pause/reset, turning assist, mobile layout; four physical boundary contacts. Software-rendered browser playback measured about 95% of real time after visual mesh reduction.\n\nSHA-256 (`isaaclab-browser-demos-v4.tar.gz`): `d0b21f7ba4d556181c3f32130a8bd1a456f16b3de2c2fff5cd8d810b9a159abf`.\n", "title": "isaac-sim/IsaacLab Browser demos v4", "topics": ["robot_learnin